      "source": [
        "# Used-car case study — no CSV input\n",
        "Run cells in order in Colab or Jupyter. Raw scraped records become `cars_df` directly in memory. **No CSV upload or CSV loading is used.**\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook keeps three models (Ridge, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting), raw vs preprocessed vs PCA comparisons, validation, small tuning searches, EDA, diagnostics and conclusions. Keep your existing Tableau/Power BI dashboards unchanged.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Collection options:** `live` requests public pages; `html` reads original vehicle webpage HTML that you save normally in your browser. `memory` uses `cars_df` or `cars_data` already collected in the current runtime. A notebook file's saved table outputs do not restore its variables.\n",
        "\n",
        "A website can refuse live requests with HTTP 403. No code here bypasses that refusal. If live access fails, switch to `html`, or run from a connection where the source allows access. Saved HTML must contain real original listing data; cleaned dashboard data is not raw evidence.\n",
        "\n",
        "The code has been checked using synthetic modelling data and sample HTML. Actual scores require your collected records. The report and presentation are separate deliverables."
      ]
    },
