        "Exclude the target from predictors. Names, URLs, descriptions, empty VINs and constant metadata are not used as predictors.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0bfa237a"
      },
      "id": "0bfa237a",
      "source": [
        "num_cols = [\"year\", \"kilometres\", \"seating_capacity\"]\n",
        "cat_cols = [\"brand\", \"model\", \"owners\", \"color\",\n",
        "            \"transmission\", \"fuel_type\", \"body_type\"]\n",
        "features = num_cols + cat_cols\n",
        "source = cars_df.copy()\n"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 16
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2c6a1070"
      },
      "id": "2c6a1070",
      "source": [
        "## 4. Remove repeated listings\n",
        "Only repeated nonblank URLs are removed. Missing URLs do not identify one shared car. Different listings can still describe the same physical car.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3813cf3b",
        "outputId": "1f5ad119-b681-4bd6-94fe-c6545ea2cc6e"
      },
      "id": "3813cf3b",
      "source": [
        "if \"url\" in source:\n",
        "    url = source[\"url\"].fillna(\"\").astype(str).str.strip()\n",
        "    source = source.loc[~(url.ne(\"\") & url.duplicated())]\n",
        "print(\"Repeated listing rows removed:\", len(cars_df) - len(source))\n"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Repeated listing rows removed: 0\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 17
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "18beaf96"
      },
      "id": "18beaf96",
      "source": [
        "## 5. Basic conversion and target checks\n",
        "Both comparison arms need these steps. Unknown or nonpositive prices cannot be training targets. A high luxury-car price is not automatically an error.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c76a9a99",
        "outputId": "f3361980-452f-4abb-908b-3fc38735bf45"
      },
      "id": "c76a9a99",
      "source": [
        "data = source[features + [\"price\"]].copy()\n",
        "for col in num_cols + [\"price\"]:\n",
        "    data[col] = pd.to_numeric(data[col], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "data = data.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",
        "for col in cat_cols:\n",
        "    data[col] = data[col].map(lambda x: str(x) if pd.notna(x) else np.nan)\n",
        "data = data.loc[data.price.notna() & data.price.gt(0)].copy()\n",
        "print(\"Usable rows:\", len(data))\n",
        "assert len(data) >= 30, \"At least 30 usable rows are needed.\"\n"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Usable rows: 1171\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 18
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dbd3782b"
      },
      "id": "dbd3782b",
      "source": [
        "## 6. Fix the train/test split\n",
        "All nine experiments use the same 80% training and 20% test cars. Learned preprocessing stays inside the training pipelines.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ff49bf16",
        "outputId": "2e05cf95-d08c-4665-9ef9-c8e296657a9a"
      },
      "id": "ff49bf16",
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    data[features], data[\"price\"], test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "print(\"Training cars:\", len(X_train))\n",
        "print(\"Test cars:\", len(X_test))\n"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Training cars: 936\n",
            "Test cars: 235\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 19
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e272a379"
      },
      "id": "e272a379",
      "source": [
        "## 7. Validate values and standardize text\n",
        "Invalid numeric predictors become missing and are imputed later. This rule uses no fitted statistics. No valid price outliers are deleted.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7e887d53"
      },
      "id": "7e887d53",
      "source": [
        "def clean_features(frame):\n",
        "    frame = frame.copy()\n",
        "    frame.loc[~frame[\"year\"].between(1900, REFERENCE_YEAR), \"year\"] = np.nan\n",
        "    frame.loc[frame[\"kilometres\"] < 0, \"kilometres\"] = np.nan\n",
        "    frame.loc[~frame[\"seating_capacity\"].between(1, 20), \"seating_capacity\"] = np.nan\n",
        "    for c in cat_cols:\n",
        "        frame[c] = frame[c].map(\n",
        "            lambda v: str(v).strip().lower() if pd.notna(v) else np.nan)\n",
        "        frame[c] = frame[c].replace({\"\": np.nan, \"unknown\": np.nan, \"n/a\": np.nan})\n",
        "    return frame\n"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 20
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7bf58813"
      },
