        "## Statistical summary and outlier audit\n",
        "IQR flags unusual observations; it does not establish that a luxury-car listing is incorrect. Retain valid high-price cars. Learned preprocessing statistics are fitted on training folds only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 458
        },
        "id": "1622d3a1",
        "outputId": "5e381fe2-18a1-4d90-c883-ad53cbd46b9d"
      },
      "id": "1622d3a1",
      "source": [
        "eda = clean_train.copy()\n",
        "eda[\"price\"] = y_train\n",
        "display(eda[num_cols + [\"price\"]].describe().round(2))\n",
        "q1, q3 = eda[num_cols + [\"price\"]].quantile(.25), eda[num_cols + [\"price\"]].quantile(.75)\n",
        "iqr = q3 - q1\n",
        "outliers = ((eda[num_cols + [\"price\"]] < q1 - 1.5*iqr) |\n",
        "            (eda[num_cols + [\"price\"]] > q3 + 1.5*iqr)).sum()\n",
        "display(outliers.rename(\"IQR flagged training rows\").to_frame())"
